   "subject": "Shiny app on AWS-EC2 - Problem having access to a database",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi All!<div><br></div><div>I have a shiny app on aws-EC2 and I need to connect to aws-RDS to load my data on my app. The app is working on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388895064000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06IYMCgKDke_t04tSW5gx0\">shinyapps.io</a>, on my laptop and also when I the run the app on Rstudio on aws-EC2. But when I try to have access to my app via <a href=\"http://35.182.36.104:3838/AVM_app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://35.182.36.104:3838/AVM_app&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388895064000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2qHsH4O4XWffyN5zjecX1j\">http://35.182.36.104:3838/AVM_app</a> I get this error: <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>ERROR: An error has occurred. Check your logs or contact the app author for clarification.</i></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\">I assume it&#39;s a problem related to the database because the app works when I load the dataset on the server (not really an option in the future).</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">library(shiny)\r\nlibrary(dplyr)\r\nlibrary(DBI)\r\nlibrary(pool)\r\nlibrary(ggplot2)\r\nlibrary(leaflet)\r\nlibrary(shinyBS)\r\nlibrary(shinythemes)\r\nlibrary(reshape2)\r\nlibrary(htmlwidgets)\r\n#library(webshot)\r\nlibrary(shinyjs)\r\nlibrary(lubridate)\r\nlibrary(sp)\r\nlibrary(RColorBrewer)\r\nlibrary(rhandsontable)\r\nlibrary(ggpubr)\r\nlibrary(dbplyr)\r\nlibrary(RMySQL)\r\n#\r\n#\r\nmy_db &lt;- dbPool(\r\n  RMySQL::MySQL(), \r\n  dbname = &quot;xx&quot;,\r\n  host = &quot;xx&quot;,\r\n  username = &quot;xx&quot;,\r\n  password = &quot;xx&quot;\r\n)\r\n#I also tried this option\r\n#my_db &lt;- src_mysql(host = &quot;xx&quot;, dbname = &quot;xx&quot;, port=3306, user=&quot;xx&quot;, password=&quot;xx&quot;)\r\n#\r\n#data_FT &lt;- tbl(my_db, &quot;BC_FULL_FT&quot;) %&gt;% select(Municipality, Lon, Lat, SalePrice, Year_sale, Month_sale, Pcode)\r\n#BC_FT &lt;- collect(data_FT, n = Inf) \r\n#\r\nBC_FT &lt;- my_db %&gt;% tbl(&quot;BC_FULL_FT&quot;) %&gt;% select(Municipality, Lon, Lat, SalePrice, Year_sale, Month_sale, Pcode) %&gt;% collect(n = Inf)\r\n#</span></font><br></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">...</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">any suggestions would be appreciated!</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">Martin</span></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "iDkefp71BAAJ",
   "from": "Greg L",
   "author": "48725385c294169f",
   "date": "2017-09-11T20:03:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: Shiny app on AWS-EC2 - Problem having access to a database",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">SSH in to your EC2 instance and check the application error logs to see what happened. That&#39;ll be more effective than trying to guess.<div><br></div><div>See docs for where to find these logs: <a href=\"http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/#logging-and-analytics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/%23logging-and-analytics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388895064000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2siFOKV7SQtHRiFnL90G55\">http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/#logging-and-analytics</a></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
