  {
   "id": "Q8a00bz8BAAJ",
   "from": "Greg L",
   "author": "48725385c294169f",
   "date": "2017-09-11T22:14:01Z",
   "subject": "Re: Shiny app on AWS-EC2 - Problem having access to a database",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Could it be a permissions issue? If your shiny-server.conf has <span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,255)\">run_as</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-size:14px\"> shiny</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,255)\">;</span>, it might not be able to run an app in <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">/home/user/</font> for example. Where&#39;s your app located, and what user is shiny server running as?<div><br><div><a href=\"http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/#run_as\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/%23run_as&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388895068000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2joeAHkzFJx9JI9NMsg2L9\">http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/#run_as</a><br><div><br></div><div><div><div><br></div><div>Also just confirming, your app runs fine on that server without Shiny Server right? I missed that before.</div><div><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "5YokjXcqBQAJ",
