     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">so I fixed my problem using <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12.8px;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">src_mysql() instead of </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12.8px;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">dbPool() and also </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:12.8px;white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:arial,sans-serif\">by not loading the library pool.</span></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">thanks!</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">Martin</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Tue, Sep 12, 2017 at 8:11 AM, Martin Lavoie <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">martin2...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">it looks like it is a permission issue with the database. If I am using a local file on the server I have access to my app <span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:12.8px\">via </span><a href=\"http://35.182.36.104:3838/AVM_app\" style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://35.182.36.104:3838/AVM_app&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388895071000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3MdmpQVsfex50g6-sULs3y\">http://35.182.36.104:3838/AVM_app</a></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">in the shiny-server.conf the user is run_as shiny<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">my app is located in /srv/shiny-server/AVM_app</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">and yes my app runs fine on that server</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">strange...</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">thanks!</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:&quot;arial narrow&quot;,sans-serif;color:rgb(7,55,99)\">M.</div></font></span></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Sep 11, 2017 at 6:14 PM, Greg L <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggll...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Could it be a permissions issue? If your shiny-server.conf has <span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,255)\">run_as</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-size:14px\"> shiny</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-size:14px;color:rgb(0,0,255)\">;</span>, it might not be able to run an app in <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">/home/user/</font> for example. Where&#39;s your app located, and what user is shiny server running as?<div><br><div><a href=\"http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/#run_as\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/%23run_as&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792388895071000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3jDEnkjzQpuw_1In4GP04Z\">http://docs.rstudio.com/shiny-server/#run_as</a><br><div><br></div><div><div><div><br></div><div>Also just confirming, your app runs fine on that server without Shiny Server right? I missed that before.</div><div><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><span>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to a topic in the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this topic, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/topic/shiny-discuss/qih7pDktD8I/unsubscribe\" target=\"_